<% content_for :title, "Skeleton" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Components</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Skeleton</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    A decorative loading placeholder. Shape it with <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">class:</code>
    — height, width and radius all come from the caller.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="skeleton-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted flex flex-wrap items-start justify-center gap-8 p-12 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
    <%= render Ui::SkeletonComponent.new(class: "size-12 rounded-full") %>
    <div class="grid gap-2">
      <%= render Ui::SkeletonComponent.new(class: "h-4 w-40") %>
      <%= render Ui::SkeletonComponent.new(class: "h-4 w-24") %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2">
    <%= render Ui::SkeletonComponent.new(class: "h-32 w-56 rounded-xl") %>
    <%= render Ui::SkeletonComponent.new(class: "h-4 w-40") %>
    <%= render Ui::SkeletonComponent.new(class: "h-4 w-28") %>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#skeleton-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="skeleton-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_skeleton_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["class", "String", "nil", "Merged over the default classes with tailwind_merge — set size and shape here (h-*, w-*, rounded-*)."],
        ["…",     "Any",    "—",   "Every other keyword (id:, data:, aria:, …) is forwarded to the root element."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Notes %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Notes</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 list-disc list-inside">
  <li>Purely decorative: the root carries <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">aria-hidden="true"</code> so screen readers skip it. Put a visually hidden "Loading…" label on the real content it stands in for, not on the skeleton itself.</li>
  <li>The pulse animation stops under <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code>, so it never becomes unwanted motion for someone who's asked for less.</li>
  <li>No Stimulus controller. Swap it for the real content once it's loaded.</li>
</ul>
